    logP = 0.3);
  annotation (Documentation(info = "<html><body><p>Diclofenamide is a carbonic anhydrase inhibitor used to treat glaucoma and to manage hyperkalemic and hypokalemic periodic paralysis. It is an approved medicine, though a marketing application for one product in the European Union was withdrawn.</p><p><small>Summary written by glm-5.3-flash from <a href=\"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q3706987\">Wikidata Q3706987</a> and the WHO ATC classification and the EMA medicines list; not checked by a person.</small></p><table><tr><td>name:</td><td>diclofenamide</td></tr><tr><td>ATC codes:</td><td>S01EC02</td></tr><tr><td>DrugBank:</td><td><a href=\"https://go.drugbank.com/drugs/DB01144\">DB01144</a></td></tr><tr><td>PubChem CID:</td><td><a href=\"https://pubchem.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/compound/3038\">3038</a></td></tr><tr><td>ChEBI:</td><td><a href=\"https://www.ebi.ac.uk/chebi/searchId.do?chebiId=CHEBI:101085\">101085</a></td></tr><tr><td>Wikidata:</td><td><a href=\"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q3706987\">Q3706987</a></td></tr><tr><td>formula:</td><td>C6H6Cl2N2O4S2</td></tr><tr><td>molar mass:</td><td>305.144 g/mol (PubChem CID 3038)</td></tr><tr><td>logP:</td><td>0.3 (Drugs.Common 25.09, not verified)</td></tr></table></body></html>"));
